WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:22.100
In the Frame, by Polly Sweetman. 

00:22.200 --> 00:27.100
It is the end of Lisa and Alice's holiday.

00:27.300 --> 00:30.100
They are leaving the Hotel Oracle.

00:30.200 --> 00:32.400
They are leaving Greece.

00:32.500 --> 00:35.700
They are going to the airport.

00:35.800 --> 00:38.400
They are going home.

00:38.500 --> 00:44.500
Goodbye, Kostas! Goodbye, Eleni!
 
00:44.600 --> 00:47.550
Thank you for our wonderful holiday!

00:47.600 --> 00:50.400
Come back to this island next year!

00:50.500 --> 00:59.200
Lisa and Alice are on the airport bus.

00:59.300 --> 01:02.200
The bus is stopping at another hotel.

01:02.300 --> 01:05.700
Some people are outside the hotel.

01:05.800 --> 01:08.800
They are going to the airport too.

01:08.900 --> 01:15.300
Look at that poor woman!

01:15.400 --> 01:18.400
She has two small children.

01:18.500 --> 01:21.500
She has a lot of luggage.

01:21.600 --> 01:23.600
And she has a pushchair.

01:23.700 --> 01:25.400
Let's help her.

01:25.760 --> 01:30.700
Lisa and Alice help the woman with her luggage.

01:30.800 --> 01:33.900
They help her with the pushchair.

01:33.700 --> 01:36.200
They help her with her children.

01:36.40 --> 01:47.900
I'm Lisa and this is my friend, Alice.

01:48.000 --> 01:51.200
Thank you, Lisa. Thank you, Alice.
 
01:51.300 --> 01:53.800
My name is Vera Brown.

01:53.900 --> 01:57.700
My children's names are Peter and Helen.

02:02.000 --> 02:08.000
I'm very worried. My husband is ill.
 
02:08.200 --> 02:12.100
He is in England. I must go to him.
 
02:12.200 --> 02:13.800
I'm going home.

02:13.900 --> 02:16.600
That's very sad news.

02:16.700 --> 02:18.400
I'm sorry, Vera.

02:18.500 --> 02:21.310
We're going to England too.

02:21.400 --> 02:23.800
We'll help you.

02:23.900 --> 02:27.870
Lisa and Alice are on the plane.

02:27.920 --> 02:30.700
Vera is on the plane too.

02:30.800 --> 02:33.400
She is sitting with her children.

02:33.500 --> 02:37.000
Look at this newspaper.

02:37.100 --> 02:39.500
Do you remember this painting?

02:39.600 --> 02:45.810
Yes. It's a painting from the island's museum!
 
02:45.900 --> 02:48.600
The artist is French.

02:48.700 --> 02:52.300
He's a famous French painter.

02:52.400 --> 02:58.900
The passengers are leaving the plane.

02:59.000 --> 03:04.100
Here we are in England, Vera.

03:04.200 --> 03:10.030
We'll help you at the airport. Thank you. You are very kind.
 
03:10.400 --> 03:15.550
Lisa, Alice and Vera are in the airport.

03:15.600 --> 03:18.840
Alice is getting their luggage.

03:23.000 --> 03:25.400
This is our last bag.

03:25.500 --> 03:27.900
Now we have everything.

03:28.000 --> 03:30.800
Now we must go to Customs.

03:30.900 --> 03:35.390
Please, I must go to the toilet!

03:35.440 --> 03:40.030
Vera is taking Peter to the toilet.

03:40.080 --> 03:42.400
Don't worry, Vera.

03:42.500 --> 03:44.200
I'll stay here.

03:44.300 --> 03:46.150
I'll stay with your luggage.

03:46.300 --> 03:48.900
Oh, thank you, Alice!

03:49.100 --> 03:53.300
Lisa, please go through Customs with Helen.

03:53.400 --> 03:57.750
Wait for Alice and me in the cafe. OK.
 
03:57.800 --> 04:00.150
Vera is at Customs.

04:00.200 --> 04:04.230
A customs officer is searching her luggage.

04:04.280 --> 04:08.110
Alice hears two customs officers talking.

04:08.160 --> 04:11.000
She is surprised.

04:13.040 --> 04:15.900
That is Vera Brownlow.

04:16.100 --> 04:18.000
She's an art thief!

04:18.100 --> 04:21.700
She steals paintings. Yes.
 
04:21.800 --> 04:24.870
But there are no paintings in her luggage.

04:24.920 --> 04:31.100
Oh! A painting is missing from the island's museum.

04:31.200 --> 04:33.810
And Vera is a thief!

04:34.000 --> 04:36.600
I must talk to these men. 

04:42.700 --> 04:48.190
There's Alice! But where is Vera?
  
04:48.240 --> 04:50.870
Is she all right?

04:50.920 --> 04:54.000
Is Peter all right?

04:54.120 --> 04:57.870
Vera comes into the cafe.

04:57.920 --> 05:01.000
She is holding Peter's hand.

05:01.100 --> 05:04.400
Here we are at last!

05:04.500 --> 05:08.800
The customs officers are searching many travellers today.

05:08.900 --> 05:11.800
I'll take Helen and the pushchair now.

05:11.900 --> 05:14.100
My sister is going to meet me.

05:14.300 --> 05:17.230
She will help me with my luggage.

05:17.280 --> 05:23.270
Suddenly, there are customs officers and police officers in the cafe.
 
05:23.320 --> 05:26.990
One officer is searching the pushchair.

05:27.040 --> 05:29.950
He is looking in the frame.

05:30.000 --> 05:32.600
What is happening?

05:32.700 --> 05:36.650
Lisa, these are not Vera's children.

05:36.740 --> 05:39.200
They are her sister's children.

05:39.300 --> 05:41.710
Vera is an art thief.

05:41.760 --> 05:45.600
Do you remember the island's museum?

05:45.700 --> 05:48.310
Do you remember the stolen painting?

05:48.360 --> 05:56.000
The customs officers are looking for the stolen painting.

05:56.120 --> 06:00.310
The customs officers have the stolen painting.

06:00.360 --> 06:03.270
They are very pleased.

06:03.320 --> 06:06.190
Vera's sister has her children.

06:06.240 --> 06:09.190
She is very pleased, too.

06:09.240 --> 06:12.600
Well done, Lisa and Alice!

06:12.700 --> 06:15.500
There is a big reward for this painting.

06:15.600 --> 06:17.300
You'll get the money.

06:17.400 --> 06:19.100
That's great!

06:19.200 --> 06:22.330
We'll go on another holiday next year.

06:22.480 --> 06:34.000
LAUGHTER
